Core Changes
This is a substantial development PR that transforms the Balaji CRM from a basic quotation/invoice tracker into a fully-featured business management system. Key architectural additions include:

1. New Pages & Navigation
/approved - Dedicated approved customers & jobs view with Excel export
/visits - Customer visits & approval queue management
/notifications - Centralized notification hub for enquiries, approvals, and payment reminders
/owner - Financial analytics with profit/expense tracking (requires password protection)
/settings - Dashboard customization, workspace branding, and data management
/help - Comprehensive user guide with FAQ and workflow documentation
2. State Management Overhaul
New settingsSlice.ts Redux reducer for dashboard customization:
Dashboard widget visibility toggles
Management panel selection
Status filter configuration
Workspace branding (customizable company name)
Enhanced recordsSlice.ts with:
Expense tracking (labor, material, transport, other categories)
Improved payment validation
New selector with memoization for performance
3. Financial & Expense Tracking
New Expense type in types.ts with category support
/owner page featuring:
Revenue vs. expense trend charts (using Recharts)
Job profitability analysis
Expense ledger with edit/delete functionality
Monthly financial summaries
4. Workflow Enhancements
Approved status added to job pipeline:
New state between "quotation_sent" and "invoiced"
Customers approve quotations before work begins
Prevents auto-invoice creation; requires explicit user action
Enhanced quotation logic:
Can reopen requests (toggle to "request_closed")
Clear approval workflow
Better state transitions
5. UI/UX Improvements
Header redesign (components/TopNav.tsx):
Branded navigation bar with logo/subtitle
Icon-based navigation
Notification badge with unread count
Mobile hamburger menu
User avatar display
Password-protected pages (ProtectedPage.tsx):
Daily access code (date-based: DDXXXXXX format)
Lockout after 5 failed attempts (30-minute cooldown)
Settings & owner finance require authentication
Enhanced CSS for header, buttons, and responsiveness
